IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 42 to 49: WORK-SHARING BENEFITS.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Work-sharing benefits are paid under s 24 of the Act (piece ei2) to a claimant working reduced hours under a
-- work-sharing agreement approved by the Commission. These regulations adapt the ordinary rules to them.
-- Out of range: s 24 (work-sharing, ei2), s 12 (regular benefits, ei1), s 13 (the waiting period, ei1), s 14 (the
-- rate of weekly benefits, ei1), s 19(1) and (2) (deduction of earnings, ei1), s 10(8)(a) and 10(12) to (15)
-- (the end and the extension of the benefit period, ei1), ss 22 and 23 (maternity and parental benefits, ei1).
-- Whether an agreement is approved, and whether employment is work-sharing employment, are facts the Commission
-- has settled: inputs.

§ `Regulation 42 -- work-sharing benefits are payable`

-- Work-sharing benefits are payable to a claimant employed in work-sharing employment for each week of
-- unemployment that falls in a benefit period established for the claimant. "Subject to sections 43 to 49, the Act
-- and any regulations made under the Act apply to the claimant, with such modifications as the circumstances
-- require": a direction to read the other rules with the changes regs 43 to 49 make; it adds no condition of its own.
-- src:746 | 42 Work-sharing benefits are payable to a claimant who is employed in work-sharing employment for each week of unemployment that falls in a benefit period established for the claimant, and subject to sections 43 to 49, the Act and any regulations made under the Act apply to the claimant, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 42 (src:746)
GIVEN `the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week falls in a benefit period established for the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 42 work-sharing benefits are payable for the week` IF
        `the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment`
    AND `the week is a week of unemployment`
    AND `the week falls in a benefit period established for the claimant`

§ `Regulation 43 -- the interruption of earnings`

-- An interruption of earnings occurs, for a person employed in work-sharing employment, at the beginning of the
-- week in which there is a reduction of at least 10 per cent in the person's normal weekly earnings. A person
-- with no normal weekly earnings has no reduction to measure: NOTHING.
-- src:747 | 43 An interruption of earnings occurs, in respect of a person employed in work-sharing employment, at the beginning of the week in which there is a reduction of at least 10 per cent in the person's normal weekly earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 43 (src:747)
GIVEN `the person's normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 43 the reduction in the person's normal weekly earnings is at least 10 per cent` IS
    IF `the person's normal weekly earnings` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`the person's normal weekly earnings` MINUS `the person's earnings for the week`) AT LEAST (10% TIMES `the person's normal weekly earnings`))

-- The interruption occurs "at the beginning of the week": the Sunday that begins the week.
-- src:747 | 43 An interruption of earnings occurs, in respect of a person employed in work-sharing employment, at the beginning of the week in which there is a reduction of at least 10 per cent in the person's normal weekly earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 43 (src:747)
GIVEN `a day in the week in which the reduction occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 43 the day on which the interruption of earnings occurs` IS
    `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `a day in the week in which the reduction occurs`

§ `Regulations 44 to 46 -- entitlement, the benefit period, the waiting period`

-- A claimant is not entitled to work-sharing benefits for any week for which they claim benefits under s 12.
-- src:748 | 44 A claimant is not entitled to work-sharing benefits for any week for which the claimant claims benefits under section 12 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 44 (src:748)
GIVEN `the claimant claims benefits under section 12 of the Act for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 44 the claimant is not entitled to work-sharing benefits for the week` IF
    `the claimant claims benefits under section 12 of the Act for the week`

-- The benefit period is extended by the total of the weeks in it in which the claimant is employed in
-- work-sharing employment, and ss 10(12) to (15) of the Act apply (those limits are piece ei1's, not applied here).
-- src:749 | 45 Where a benefit period has been established in respect of a claimaint and for any week during that benefit period the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment, the benefit period shall be extended by the total of those weeks and subsections 10(12) to (15) of the Act apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 45 (src:749)
GIVEN `the weeks of the benefit period in which the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 45 the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` IS
    `the weeks of the benefit period in which the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment`

-- src:749 | 45 Where a benefit period has been established in respect of a claimaint and for any week during that benefit period the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment, the benefit period shall be extended by the total of those weeks and subsections 10(12) to (15) of the Act apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 45 (src:749)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`
      `the weeks of the benefit period in which the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `reg 45 the benefit period as extended` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period`, (`the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` PLUS (`weeks as days` (`reg 45 the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` `the weeks of the benefit period in which the claimant is employed in work-sharing employment`)))

-- If the claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment and the waiting period has not been served as
-- s 13 requires, or earnings have not been deducted as s 19(1) requires, the serving of the period or the
-- deduction is deferred until that employment has terminated.
-- src:750 | 46 If a claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment and the waiting period has not been served as required by section 13 of the Act or earnings have not been deducted as required by subsection 19(1) of the Act, the serving of the period or the deduction of the earnings shall be deferred until that employment has terminated.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 46 (src:750)
GIVEN `the claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work-sharing employment has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waiting period has not been served as required by section 13 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 46 the serving of the waiting period is deferred` IF
        `the claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment`
    AND `the waiting period has not been served as required by section 13 of the Act`
    AND NOT (`the work-sharing employment has terminated`)

-- src:750 | 46 If a claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment and the waiting period has not been served as required by section 13 of the Act or earnings have not been deducted as required by subsection 19(1) of the Act, the serving of the period or the deduction of the earnings shall be deferred until that employment has terminated.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 46 (src:750)
GIVEN `the claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work-sharing employment has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `earnings have not been deducted as required by subsection 19(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 46 the deduction of earnings is deferred` IF
        `the claimant becomes employed in work-sharing employment`
    AND `earnings have not been deducted as required by subsection 19(1) of the Act`
    AND NOT (`the work-sharing employment has terminated`)

§ `Regulation 47 -- earnings`

-- (1) Earnings received for a week from work-sharing employment are not deducted from the work-sharing benefits
-- payable under s 24 of the Act.
-- src:751 | 47 (1) Earnings received for any week by a claimant from work-sharing employment shall not be deducted from the work-sharing benefits payable pursuant to section 24 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 47(1) (src:751)
GIVEN `the earnings received for the week from work-sharing employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 47(1) the amount of earnings from work-sharing employment deducted from the work-sharing benefits` IS 0

-- (2) If the claimant receives earnings for a week other than by reason of work-sharing employment, the amount
-- determined under s 19(2) of the Act is deducted from the work-sharing benefits for that week.
-- src:752 | (2) If a claimant receives earnings for any week other than by reason of work-sharing employment, the amount determined under subsection 19(2) of the Act shall be deducted from the work-sharing benefits payable to the claimant for that week.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 47(2) (src:752)
GIVEN `the claimant receives earnings for the week other than by reason of work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount determined under subsection 19(2) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 47(2) the amount deducted from the work-sharing benefits for the week` IS
    IF `the claimant receives earnings for the week other than by reason of work-sharing employment`
    THEN `the amount determined under subsection 19(2) of the Act`
    ELSE 0

§ `Regulation 48 -- the rate of weekly benefits`

-- The rate is the rate determined under s 14 of the Act multiplied by the ratio of (a) the hours, days or shifts
-- the claimant did not work because of the work-sharing agreement to (b) the hours, days or shifts they would have
-- worked on their usual schedule. The same unit is used for both. No usual schedule, no ratio: NOTHING.
-- src:753 | 48 The rate of weekly benefits payable to a claimant employed under a work-sharing agreement approved by the Commission for the purposes of section 24 of the Act is an amount that bears the same ratio to the claimant's rate of weekly benefits determined pursuant to section 14 of the Act that
-- src:754 | (a) the number of hours, days or shifts that the claimant did not work because of the work-sharing agreement
-- src:755 | bears to
-- src:756 | (b) the number of hours, days or shifts that the claimant would have worked for the employer according to the claimant's usual work schedule.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 48 (src:753-756)
GIVEN `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits determined under section 14 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours, days or shifts the claimant did not work because of the work-sharing agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours, days or shifts the claimant would have worked according to their usual work schedule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 48 the rate of weekly benefits payable under a work-sharing agreement` IS
    IF `the hours, days or shifts the claimant would have worked according to their usual work schedule` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the claimant's rate of weekly benefits determined under section 14 of the Act` TIMES (`the hours, days or shifts the claimant did not work because of the work-sharing agreement` DIVIDED BY `the hours, days or shifts the claimant would have worked according to their usual work schedule`))

§ `Regulation 49 -- weeks that do not count`

-- Work-sharing benefits are not taken into account for paragraph 10(8)(a) of the Act (the benefit period ends when
-- the maximum number of weeks under s 12 has been paid) or for determining the benefits payable under ss 22 and 23
-- of the Act. The weeks that count are the weeks of benefits paid, not counting the weeks of work-sharing benefits.
-- src:757 | 49 Work-sharing benefits shall not be taken into account for the purpose of paragraph 10(8)(a) of the Act or for determining the benefits payable under sections 22 and 23 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 49 (src:757)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of work-sharing benefits among them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 49 the weeks of benefits paid that count, not counting weeks of work-sharing benefits` IS
    max 0 (`the weeks of benefits paid` MINUS `the weeks of work-sharing benefits among them`)
